# Sprint Context Rule

## Source of Truth
`implementation-plan.md` (repo root) defines all sprints, tasks, and the CURRENT
active sprint/task in its "Current Status" section.

## At the Start of Every Task
1. Read implementation-plan.md -> find "Current Status"
2. Use the Active Sprint and Active Task for all prompt-log entries
3. If the developer's prompt references a different task ID, use that and update Current Status

## When a Task Completes
1. Mark the task [x] in implementation-plan.md
2. Update "Last Completed" and advance "Active Task"
3. Apply the prompt-history-during-task rule (using Sprint/Task IDs from here)

## When All Tasks in a Sprint Are Done (Quality Gate)
1. Confirm build/tests/docs for the sprint pass
2. Advance "Active Sprint" to the next sprint
3. Trigger the prompt-history-sprint-log rule to generate prompt-history/sprint-X.X.md

## If Current Status Is Ambiguous
Ask the developer "Which sprint/task are we on?" — do NOT guess.
